{{!-- One list, drawn by both the Petty and the Belongings tab: the two hold the
      same kind of row and differ only in which question put it there — zero slots, or not under
      direct possession — so they are one template and the eye finds every control in the same
      place on both.

      The "add" control is on the zone heading above this list, on each tab, not
      in a header row of its own here.

      A container's row is the same 26px line as anything else, and its name opens its sheet like
      every other name here. It used to be a `<details>` that unfolded to the names of what it
      held: on an empty bag that was a click that opened a blank strip, and on a full one it was
      a second, poorer view of the Contents tab the sheet already has. One row, one affordance —
      the capacity chip says how full it is, and the sheet says what is in it.

      The rule under a row is drawn ink, not a border, and it is only emitted when the row has a
      row after it — a line belongs BETWEEN two entries, and one under the last one reads as a
      second zone rule immediately above the real one.

      A row is a drop target: an item of the actor's dropped on it goes inside
      (`actor-sheet.js#_onDropItem`). The walking figure is the SET ASIDE / TAKE BACK toggle and the
      hand is EQUIPPED, as on the ten — two different questions, and a mule answers neither: it is
      in nobody's grip and was never under direct possession to begin with.

      @param rows   The item views to draw.
      @param seed   Ink seed prefix, so each zone's strokes keep their own silhouette.
      @param empty  What the zone says when it has nothing in it. --}}
<ol class="cairn-plain-list">
    {{#each rows as |row|}}
    <li class="cairn-slot draggable{{#if row.isUsedUp}} used-up{{/if}}" data-item-id="{{row.id}}"
        {{#unless @last}}data-ink="hline" data-ink-seed="{{../seed}}-{{row.id}}" data-ink-w="0.9" data-ink-a="0.42" data-ink-at="bottom"{{/unless}}>
        <div class="cairn-slot-body">
            {{!-- The name IS the affordance, as on the slot row: `itemEdit` is the pencil's
                  handler already, so the row and the pencil cannot drift apart. A container
                  carries its capacity chip here, as it does on the ten. --}}
            <span class="cairn-item-name-and-tags" data-action="itemEdit">
                <span class="cairn-item-title">{{#if row.system.equipped}}<strong>{{row.name}}</strong>{{else}}{{row.name}}{{/if}}</span>
                {{> "systems/cairn2e/templates/parts/item-tags.hbs" system=row.system}}
                {{#if row.system.isContainer}}<span class="cairn-item-tag">{{row.system.contentsSlots}}/{{row.system.capacity}}</span>{{/if}}
                {{#if row.showUses}}{{> "systems/cairn2e/templates/parts/item-uses.hbs" uses=row.usesDisplay editable=@root.editable}}{{/if}}
            </span>
        </div>
        {{> "systems/cairn2e/templates/parts/item-controls.hbs" item=row editable=@root.editable}}
    </li>
    {{else}}
    <li class="cairn-empty">{{empty}}</li>
    {{/each}}
</ol>
